# Project Conventions (Cursor Rules)

## Stack

- React (functional components only, no class components)
- Tailwind CSS for all styling (no custom CSS files unless necessary)
- Vite as build tool

## Conventions

- Commit format: Conventional Commits (e.g., `feat: add navbar component`, `fix: resolve button alignment`)
- Code style: 2-space indentation, single quotes for strings
- Components go in `src/components/`
- Keep components small and single-responsibility

## Project Rules (learned from FE-02 workflow drill)

1. Forms must use react-hook-form + zod for validation — never rely on bare HTML5 attributes (type="email", required) or hand-rolled regex validation functions as the only validation layer.
2. Every form input must have a `<label>` explicitly linked via `htmlFor`/`id` — this is a reviewable, testable requirement, not optional polish.
3. Any feature that saves user data must persist it (localStorage or API) and reload it on mount. A "Save" handler that only logs to the console (or otherwise doesn't actually persist) is a bug, not a placeholder — never ship a success message for a save that doesn't happen.